The players.csv file only has 451 players but player_box_scores references 683 unique players. This causes "Unknown Player" in embeddings.

Use the NBA API to fetch missing player data and add to players.csv:

```python
import requests
import pandas as pd

# Load existing players
existing = pd.read_csv('backend/data/players.csv')
existing_ids = set(existing['player_id'].values)

# Get unique player IDs from box scores
box_scores = pd.read_csv('backend/data/player_box_scores.csv')
all_player_ids = set(box_scores['person_id'].unique())

# Find missing
missing_ids = all_player_ids - existing_ids
print(f"Missing {len(missing_ids)} players")

# Fetch from NBA API
new_players = []
for player_id in missing_ids:
    url = f"https://stats.nba.com/stats/commonplayerinfo?PlayerID={player_id}"
    headers = {
        "User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0",
        "Referer": "https://www.nba.com/"
    }
    resp = requests.get(url, headers=headers)
    data = resp.json()
    
    if data['resultSets'][0]['rowSet']:
        row = data['resultSets'][0]['rowSet'][0]
        new_players.append({
            'player_id': player_id,
            'first_name': row[1],
            'last_name': row[2],
            'team_id': row[18] or 0,
            'draft_year': row[28] or 0
        })

# Combine and save
new_df = pd.DataFrame(new_players)
combined = pd.concat([existing, new_df], ignore_index=True)
combined.to_csv('backend/data/players.csv', index=False)
print(f"Updated players.csv: {len(combined)} total players")
```

